n   \\]\n\n4. **Convert the fraction to a percentage:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{4} \\times 100 = 25\\%\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage tip Patty gave is \\(\\boxed{25}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{25}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:12"}
